          "status": "needs-review",
          "text": "Description: Two witnesses observed on January 09, 2009 at 21:29, a round object that appeared stationary in the sky heading S-SE. One witness noted a change in color. Only one email testimony is recorded at GEIPAN. The mentioned photo is not attached to the email. The observation could correspond to the star SIRIUS, observable in the full southeast, whose color changes are characteristic. However, the lack of information gathered from the witness does not allow this hypothesis to be fully validated. This case is classified in category C: Lack of Information.",
